This is an illustrative Flask-style structure. Django uses its own project and app conventions.

### Architecture Rules
1. Keep routes separate from analytical calculations.
2. Keep database operations separate from business logic.
3. Validate uploaded datasets.
4. Test analytical functions independently.
5. Use structured JSON responses.
6. Protect user data and permissions.
7. Handle errors and missing records.
8. Avoid processing huge datasets entirely in memory.
9. Use pagination, caching and background jobs when needed.
10. Verify analytical outputs against known results.
11. Keep secrets in environment variables.
12. Use database transactions where business operations require consistency.
13. Use logging and automated tests.
14. Document deployment and backup procedures.

